ssed to Cruz in the  final film as although smokey explained  that the rules only say the number has  to be out there doesn't say who has to  wear it the confusion is initially  created meant this transition wasn't  quite as smooth as I would have liked  the car three filmmakers obviously spent  a lot of time considering all possible  options but I still wonder whether there  was another way to have done this it  didn't raise quite so many questions in  my mind while I was watching the movie  what did you think about the ending did  you enjoy it  or would you prefer to see something  different by the way there are some  interesting storyboards which hinted a  deleted scene or another alternate  ending where McQueen reveals his  transformation into the fabulous  Lightning McQueen at the Piston Cup race  rather than at the very end of the movie  you can see him emerging with Doc's  colors in the number 51 to a group of  press then the crowd and finally onto  the track where he faces up to Jackson's  storm in the final movie the reveal of  the fabulous Lightning McQueen is a much  more private moment for lightning with  his friends at Radiator Springs  although the movies final scene of  lightning and veining his own marsh to  doc Hudson was lovely these storyboards  hint that the filmmakers considered a  much more dramatic and symbolic way of  bringing doc back to life through his  protege to quote story supervisor Scott  Morse my having lightning announces new  number and colors at the  and cup I'm not sure this would have fit  the way the rest of the ending played  out for perhaps fans of Doc Hudson  especially would have enjoyed seeing  this scene production on car three began  at Pixar in 2013 but it wasn't until  2015 the final direction of the story  was decided on after John Lasseter was  inspired by the retirement of his friend  professional NASCAR racer Jeff Gordon at  the age of 43 which means that during  those two years various fascinating  ideas and stori